        { sender: "user", text: "how does backprop calculate gradients?" },
        { sender: "buddy", text: "It uses the recursive chain rule layer-by-layer backwards through the network to update weights.<br><br>Want to look at the math in Chapter 6?" },
        { sender: "user", text: "yes" },
        { sender: "buddy", text: "<div class='illustration-card'><div class='ill-cover-fallback dl'><div class='fallback-cover-text'>Deep Learning</div></div><div class='ill-text'><span class='ill-title'>Deep Learning Book</span><span class='ill-author'>Ian Goodfellow et al.</span><span class='ill-meta'>Ch 6 · 12.4k words</span></div></div><br><br>I've opened the chapter in the reader and highlighted the recursive equations." },
        { sender: "user", text: "show me the equations" },
        { sender: "buddy", text: "<div class='wb-chat-card'><div class='wb-chat-icon'><svg width='12' height='12' viewBox='0 0 24 24' fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='2.5'><path d='M2 3h20'></path><path d='M21 3v11a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V3'></path><path d='m7 21 5-5 5 5'></path></svg></div><div class='wb-chat-title-group'><div class='wb-chat-title'>Whiteboard</div><div class='wb-chat-subtitle'>Backprop derivatives</div></div></div><br><br>Sure, I'll calculate and render the derivatives on your whiteboard." }
